---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PricingCard from '../components/PricingCard.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Pricing — OpsHQ Digital"
  description="Transparent pricing for AI Inbox and custom work. No hidden fees, no annual contracts."
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="bg-navy-950 text-white py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-6">Simple, Honest Pricing</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-300">One productized service. One transparent number. Plus custom-scope work at fair hourly rates.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Productized -->
  <section class="py-16 md:py-20">
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-center gap-2 mb-4">
        <div class="w-2 h-2 bg-blue-500 rounded-full"></div>
        <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-blue-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Productized Service</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-950 mb-8 text-center">AI Inbox</h2>
      <PricingCard
        productName="AI Inbox for Wedding Venues"
        monthlyFee="$649"
        setupFee="$0"
        pilotOffer="30-day free pilot — full refund if you cancel before day 31"
        features={[
          "Custom AI assistant trained on your venue's voice + pricing + packages",
          "Inquiry monitoring across Microsoft 365 or Google Workspace",
          "5-minute first-response SLA",
          "Human-in-the-loop approval via mobile push",
          "Calendar integration for tour booking",
          "Direct support from Nick — no ticket queue",
          "Audit log of every draft, edit, approval, and send",
          "Cancel anytime with 30-day notice; clean data export",
        ]}
        ctaText="Start Free Pilot"
        ctaHref="/contact/?service=ai-inbox"
        footnote="Want this for photographers, planners, or caterers? We're expanding to adjacent verticals in 2026 — let's talk."
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Custom work -->
  <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-slate-50">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4">
        <div class="w-2 h-2 bg-blue-500 rounded-full"></div>
        <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-blue-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Custom Work</span>
      </div>
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-navy-950 mb-6">Everything Else: Fair Rates, Fixed-Scope When Possible</h2>
      <div class="text-slate-700 space-y-4 text-lg leading-relaxed">
        <p>Most custom work falls into one of these buckets:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-3">
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-blue-500 mt-1.5">•</span> <span><strong>Discovery + scoping:</strong> Free 30-minute discovery call. Written scope + fixed quote within 3 business days.</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-blue-500 mt-1.5">•</span> <span><strong>Fixed-scope build:</strong> $4,500–$25,000 depending on complexity. Half up front, half on delivery.</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-blue-500 mt-1.5">•</span> <span><strong>Time-and-materials:</strong> $175/hr for ongoing maintenance, small tweaks, or projects where scope can't be fixed in advance.</span></li>
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="text-blue-500 mt-1.5">•</span> <span><strong>Retainer:</strong> $1,200/mo for 8 prioritized hours, rollover up to 16 hours. Good fit for businesses that need a developer "on call" but not full-time.</span></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="pt-4">See <a href="/capabilities/" class="text-blue-500 font-medium hover:underline">the capabilities page</a> for what we typically build.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-10">
        <a href="/contact/?service=custom" class="inline-flex items-center px-8 py-4 bg-blue-500 hover:bg-blue-600 text-white font-medium rounded-lg transition-colors text-lg min-h-[44px]">
          Book a Discovery Call →
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
